t the blocks!":"sh-card-b1","Fill the Right Block!":"sh-card-b2","Add and Subtract!":"sh-card-l2","Add and Take Away! Column style!":"sh-card-c1","Times Table chart! Tap a square!":"sh-card-m2","Read Big Numbers! Build a big one!":"sh-card-r1","Read Fractions! Tap the pieces!":"sh-card-f1","Count By! Count in jumps!":"sh-card-s1","Carry and Borrow! For big kids!":"sh-card-c2","Which is Bigger? Feed the hungry mouth!":"sh-card-g1","What's Missing? Make both sides the same!":"sh-card-b3","Odd or Even? Pair them up!":"sh-card-oe1","Make 10! Fill it up, or watch them fly!":"sh-card-n1","Make 100! How many more make a hundred?":"sh-card-n3","Hundred Board! Where do you land?":"sh-card-h1","Share It Out! Deal them fairly!":"sh-card-d1","What's the Fraction? Count the lit parts!":"sh-card-q1","Which Unit? Tap a picture!":"sh-card-u1","Cover It! How many squares?":"sh-card-a1","Number Toys! Build your own number sentence!":"sh-card-np1","Memory Match! Turn two over and find the pairs!":"sh-card-k1","Sequence! Complete the number pattern!":"sh-card-sq1","Multiply! Column style!":"sh-card-c5","You reached Earth!":"sh-arrive-0","Earth is our home planet — the only place we know with oceans, trees and you!":"sh-fact-0","Earth spins all the way round once every day. That is what makes morning and night!":"sh-fact-0-2","Water covers most of the Earth. From space, our planet looks blue!":"sh-fact-0-3","Earth has a blanket of air all around it, and that air is what you breathe.":"sh-fact-0-4","You reached the Moon!":"sh-arrive-1","Footprints on the Moon never blow away, because the Moon has no wind at all!":"sh-fact-1","The Moon has no light of its own. It shines because the Sun shines on it!":"sh-fact-1-2","On the Moon you would weigh much less, so you could jump ever so high!":"sh-fact-1-3","The Moon goes round and round the Earth, like a friend who never leaves.":"sh-fact-1-4","You reached Mars!":"sh-arrive-2","Mars is called the Red Planet, because it is covered in rusty red dust!":"sh-fact-2","Mars has two little moons. They are called Phobos and Deimos!":"sh-fact-2-2","The biggest volcano in the whole solar system is on Mars. Its name is Olympus Mons!":"sh-fact-2-3","Robots from Earth are driving about on Mars, taking photographs of the dust.":"sh-fact-2-4","You reached the Asteroid Belt!":"sh-arrive-3","The asteroid belt is full of giant space rocks, all tumbling around the Sun!":"sh-fact-3","The asteroid belt sits between Mars and Jupiter, like a ring of rubble.":"sh-fact-3-2","The biggest rock in the belt is called Ceres, and it is round like a little planet!":"sh-fact-3-3","The rocks are so far apart that a spaceship flies straight through without bumping one!":"sh-fact-3-4","You reached Jupiter!":"sh-arrive-4","Jupiter is the biggest planet of all — one thousand Earths could fit inside it!":"sh-fact-4","Jupiter has a storm called the Great Red Spot, and it is wider than the whole Earth!":"sh-fact-4-2","Jupiter is not solid like Earth. It is an enormous ball of swirling gas!":"sh-fact-4-3","Jupiter has a crowd of moons going round it — more than ninety of them!":"sh-fact-4-4","You reached Saturn!":"sh-arrive-5","Saturn’s beautiful rings are made of billions of pieces of sparkling ice!":"sh-fact-5","Saturn is so light for its size that it would float in a giant bath of water!":"sh-fact-5-2","A day on Saturn is short. It spins all the way round in about ten hours!":"sh-fact-5-3","Saturn’s biggest moon is called Titan, and it has rivers — but not rivers of water!":"sh-fact-5-4","You reached the Milky Way!":"sh-arrive-6","Our galaxy is called the Milky Way — it has more stars than you could ever count!":"sh-fact-6","Our Sun is just one star in the Milky Way, and there are billions more!":"sh-fact-6-2","From far away, the Milky Way looks like an enormous spinning pinwheel of stars.":"sh-fact-6-3","Earth, the Moon, Mars, Saturn — everywhere you have been today lives inside the Milky Way!":"sh-fact-6-4","Journey complete! You reached the Milky Way!":"sh-arrive-final","A brand new journey begins. Blast off!":"sh-journey-new","Off we go!":"sh-journey-go","What number? Count the blocks!":"sh-l-what-number-count-the-blocks","Tap again for a new one!":"sh-l-tap-again-for-a-new-one","Too many! Take one away.":"sh-l-too-many-take-one-away","The little box holds one, or nothing.":"sh-l-the-little-box-holds-one-or-nothing","Tap any square to see what it makes!":"sh-l-tap-any-square-to-see-what-it-makes","Tap the pieces to make a fraction!":"sh-l-tap-the-pieces-to-make-a-fraction","Zero.":"sh-l-zero","Which side has more?":"sh-l-which-side-has-more","The mouth opens towards the bigger number. If they are the same, it keeps its mouth shut.":"sh-l-the-mouth-opens-towards-the-bigger-number-if","Odd or even?":"sh-l-odd-or-even","Pair them up! If one is left without a partner, it is odd. If they all have a partner, it is even.":"sh-l-pair-them-up-if-one-is-left-without-a-partne","Pair them up!":"sh-l-pair-them-up","Count the rows between them. Each row is ten.":"sh-l-count-the-rows-between-them-each-row-is-ten","The row is full. One more begins the next row, at its first seat.":"sh-l-the-row-is-full-one-more-begins-the-next-row","Deal them round and round — one to this basket, one to that one. Fair shares are equal.":"sh-l-deal-them-round-and-round-one-to-this-basket","Count the counters in one basket.":"sh-l-count-the-counters-in-one-basket","See baskets in your head. Deal them out fairly — one to each.":"sh-l-see-baskets-in-your-head-deal-them-out-fairl","That share is not fair — one basket has more. Fair shares are equal. Try again!":"sh-l-that-share-is-not-fair-one-basket-has-more-f","What fraction of the objects are lit?":"sh-l-what-fraction-of-the-objects-are-lit","What fraction is highlighted?":"sh-l-what-fraction-is-highlighted","Count the lit parts for the top number. Count all the parts for the bottom number.":"sh-l-count-the-lit-parts-for-the-top-number-count","Tap a picture to hear how big it is!":"sh-l